astric carcinoma in the body of the stomach. The first marking was done on the margin of the carcinoma and then the second marking was done on the surrounding non-cancerous mucosa. (<bold>B</bold>) The mean IHb was calculated from the data of the picture elements on the described area. The C/N ratio was 1.26 (IHb-C: 37.7, IHb-N: 30.0).</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="jkms-21-1041-g004"/></fig><fig id="F5" position="float"><label>Fig. 5</label><caption><p>(<bold>A</bold>) Electronic endoscopic image of a diffuse-type gastric carcinoma in the body of the stomach. The first marking was done on the margin of the carcinoma and then the second marking was done on the surrounding non-cancerous mucosa. (<bold>B</bold>) The mean IHb was calculated from the data of the picture elements on the described area. The C/N ratio was 0.84 (IHb-C: 28.3, IHb-N: 33.6).</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="jkms-21-1041-g005"/></fig><fig id="F6" position="float"><label>Fig. 6</label><caption><p>The C/N ratio in the diffuse-type carcinoma group and in the intestinal-type carcinoma group.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="jkms-21-1041-g006"/></fig><fig id="F7" position="float"><label>Fig. 7</label><caption><p>The C/N ratio in the intestinal-type carcinoma group and in the diffuse-type carcinoma group according to the location.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="jkms-21-1041-g007"/></fig><table-wrap id="T1" position="float"><label>Table 1</label><caption><p>Results of the C/N ratio in the intestinal-type group and in the diffuse-type group according to the location of carcinoma</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="jkms-21-1041-i001"/></table-wrap></floats-group></article>